# Adobe Experience Platform React Native SDK - Project Structure

This is a **Lerna monorepo** with **Yarn workspaces** for the Adobe Experience Platform React Native SDK.

## 📁 Repository Structure

- **`packages/`** - Individual SDK packages (core, edge, messaging, etc.)
- **`apps/AEPSampleAppNewArchEnabled/`** - Expo-based sample app with New Architecture support
- **`docs/`** - Documentation and development guides
- **`tests/`** - Shared test utilities and configurations

## 🔧 Monorepo Configuration

- **Lerna**: Uses independent versioning strategy ([lerna.json](mdc:lerna.json))
- **Yarn Workspaces**: Manages dependencies across packages ([package.json](mdc:package.json))
- **TypeScript**: Strict configuration with React Native support ([tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json))

## 📦 Package Structure Pattern

Each SDK package follows this consistent structure:
```
packages/{name}/
├── package.json           # Package configuration
├── README.md             # Package documentation
├── src/
│   ├── index.ts          # Main exports
│   ├── {Name}.ts         # Primary implementation
│   └── models/           # TypeScript models/types
├── __tests__/            # Jest test files
├── android/              # Android native implementation
│   ├── build.gradle
│   └── src/main/
├── ios/                  # iOS native implementation
│   └── src/
└── RCT{Name}.podspec     # iOS CocoaPods spec
```

## 🏗️ Build Commands

- `yarn build` - Compile all packages with TypeScript
- `yarn test` - Run Jest tests across packages
- `yarn sampleappnewarchenabled:*` - Sample app commands

## 🎯 Key Files

- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Root workspace configuration
- [lerna.json](mdc:lerna.json) - Lerna monorepo settings
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration
- [jest.config.js](mdc:jest.config.js) - Testing setup
